                                     BUSINESS Question  
How does churn vary across customer segments based on contract type, internet type, tenure, and selected service features?

                                        
                                     Query
SELECT
Contract,
Internet_Type,
COUNT(*) total_customers,
SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS chunred_customers,
ROUND(SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)* 100.0/COUNT(*),2) AS churn_rate
FROM telecom_customer
GROUP BY Contract,Internet_Type
ORDER BY churn_rate DESC;

                                         INSIGHT:
The data above shows that the month-to-month contract type had the highest churn rate for all the various internet types. 

                                
                                      Possible drivers
Further analysis was made and it shows that month to month customers who did not subscribe to the key services had the highest number of churn rate suggesting that not 
having these services was associated with higher churn

SELECT
Contract,
Internet_Type,
COUNT(*) total_customers,
SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS chunred_customers,
ROUND(SUM(CASE WHEN Customer_Status ='Churned' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)* 100.0/COUNT(*),2) AS churn_rate,
CASE WHEN Online_Backup = 'Yes' THEN 1 
ELSE 0
END AS Online
FROM telecom_customer
GROUP BY Contract,Internet_Type,CASE WHEN Online_Backup = 'Yes' THEN 1 
ELSE 0
END
ORDER BY churn_rate DESC;

